1. Brand Identity Overview
Hill Country Web Works blends modern technology with Hill Country warmth. Your brand should feel:
	• Local and approachable
	• Clean and modern
	• Trustworthy and dependable
	• Technically strong without feeling corporate
	• Rooted in Texas Hill Country aesthetics
Your visual identity should reflect the balance between professional tech expertise and small‑town friendliness.
2. Color Palette
Your brand colors should reflect the Hill Country landscape and your chosen maroon/white/gray identity.
Primary Colors
Color	Hex	Usage
Maroon	#7A1E2C	Buttons, accents, headings, logo
Warm White	#F8F6F4	Backgrounds, negative space
Charcoal Gray	#2E2E2E	Body text, footer, icons
Secondary Colors
Color	Hex	Usage
Soft Gray	#D9D9D9	Borders, cards, subtle backgrounds
Hill Country Blue	#3A5F7D	Optional accent for links or highlights
Sage Green	#8A9F8C	Optional accent for nature‑themed visuals
Color Personality
	• Maroon = strength, Texas identity, confidence
	• White = clarity, simplicity
	• Gray = professionalism
	• Blue/Sage = optional touches that evoke Hill Country landscapes
3. Typography
Your fonts should be clean, modern, and easy to read.
Primary Font (Headings)
Montserrat
	• Modern, bold, trustworthy
	• Great for headings, hero text, and section titles
Secondary Font (Body Text)
Inter or Roboto
	• Clean, highly readable
	• Perfect for paragraphs, service descriptions, and UI elements
Optional Accent Font
Playfair Display
	• Use sparingly for quotes or emphasis
	• Adds a subtle, classy touch
4. Logo Direction
You don’t need a complex logo — simple and clean will serve you best.
Logo Concepts
	• A stylized HCWW monogram in maroon
	• A simple outline of the Texas Hill Country hills behind the text
	• A minimal cloud + code bracket icon
	• A maroon circle or badge with “Hill Country Web Works” around the edge
Logo Style
	• Flat design
	• No gradients
	• Strong contrast
	• Works well in monochrome
Logo Usage
	• Full logo for website header
	• Simplified icon for favicon and social media
	• Horizontal version for business cards and email signatures
5. Imagery & Photography Style
Your imagery should feel local, warm, and authentic.
Use imagery that includes:
	• Hill Country landscapes
	• Boerne Main Street
	• Local businesses
	• Clean tech setups (laptops, servers, cloud visuals)
	• Warm lighting and natural textures
Avoid:
	• Corporate stock photos
	• Overly futuristic tech imagery
	• Cold or sterile visuals
Image Tone
	• Natural
	• Warm
	• Approachable
	• Slightly rustic but modern
6. Iconography
Use simple, line‑based icons with rounded edges.
Icon Style
	• Thin line weight
	• Minimalist
	• Monochrome (charcoal or maroon)
	• Consistent stroke width
Examples
	• Globe icon for websites
	• Shield icon for security
	• Cloud icon for cloud services
	• Wrench or gear icon for troubleshooting
7. Voice & Tone Guidelines
Your brand voice should sound like you — friendly, clear, and confident.
Voice Characteristics
	• Approachable
	• Helpful
	• Straightforward
	• Technically competent
	• Calm and reassuring
Tone Examples
Do: “Let’s get your website running smoothly.” “I’ll take care of the technical details so you can focus on your business.”
Don’t: “Your DNS propagation failed due to misconfigured MX records.” (You can explain this later, but not in marketing copy.)
8. Brand Messaging Pillars
These are the core ideas your brand should communicate everywhere:
1. Local Expertise
You’re part of the community — not a faceless IT shop.
2. Enterprise‑Grade Skill
Your Microsoft and Rackspace background sets you apart.
3. Reliability
Clear communication, fast response times, and dependable support.
4. Simplicity
You make technology easy for small businesses.
5. Long‑Term Partnership
You’re not a one‑and‑done vendor — you’re their tech partner.
9. Layout & Spacing Guidelines
Your website and materials should feel clean and uncluttered.
Spacing Rules
	• Generous padding around sections
	• Plenty of white space
	• Avoid dense paragraphs
	• Use bullet points for clarity
Layout Style
	• Centered hero section
	• Two‑column layouts for services
	• Full‑width sections with alternating background colors
	• Sticky header with logo + navigation
